# archives de developpement — hors depot
docs/archive/
docs/specs/
lanceurs/archive/
scripts/archive/
config/
tests/
# app/src-tauri/tests holds the crate's integration tests. They are produced
# code, not a development scratch directory, and the bare rule above swallowed
# them: an integration test that cannot be committed cannot run in CI either,
# and its absence looks exactly like a passing build.
!app/src-tauri/tests/
# Same reasoning, one file: CMake registers this differential as a ctest
# (galactus-p0-split-differential). A checkout without it does not skip the
# test, it fails to run it, and the packer/reader agreement it proves is the
# one thing in the split chain that cannot be checked from one side alone.
!scripts/tests/
scripts/tests/*
!scripts/tests/test-p0-split-differential.py
# Same again, two more files, same reason: CMake registers them as ctest tests
# (galactus-cache-plan-differential, galactus-replay-cache-harness). The first
# is the only thing that keeps the C++ slot allocator and the Python one that
# produced every published measurement saying the same word; the second is the
# only thing that keeps the replay harness reproducing the engine to the byte.
# Neither can be checked from one side alone, and a checkout without them
# fails the test run rather than skipping it.
!scripts/tests/test-cache-plan-differential.py
!scripts/tests/test-replay-cache.py
# And the directory the bare rule above actually names. CMakeLists.txt calls
# add_executable on all three sources here and registers them as ctest tests
# (galactus-b2c-sha256-file-runtime, galactus-c1-contract-runtime,
# galactus-h4-a0-contract-runtime). A missing source is not a skipped test:
# add_executable on a file that is not there is a hard CMake configure error,
# so a fresh clone cannot even generate a build system. The fixture is listed
# too because galactus-b2c-sha256-file-runtime is invoked with its path as the
# argument, and a test that cannot find its known-answer file proves nothing.
!tests/
tests/*
!tests/*.cpp
!tests/fixtures/
PROJECT.md
galactus.env
.gstack/

